id: pm-7dsolo
title: Accept actively registered relationship kinds in SDK and CLI dependency mutations
description: "GitHub 1452 reports that registerRelationshipKinds activation succeeds, but create/update dependency assignments still refuse custom kinds through a built-in vocabulary. This blocks downstream package-defined ordering edges despite graph registry support. Reproduce in an isolated installed extension and align mutation validation, aliases and diagnostics with the active workspace registry."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T15:22:02.458Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T19:12:22.188Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#da6c4a524d0c5025cfe0e34b"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Use a real isolated extension to prove create/update and SDK writes plus graph traversal for a custom ordering kind; validate aliases and cardinality/cycle semantics through the authoritative active registry; deactivated or absent registrations refuse before item/history mutation; an independent pre-fix control fails; complete source coverage, SDK contracts and installed Node/Bun consumers pass."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: CLI and SDK dependency writes accept active registered kinds and aliases while refusing inactive or unknown kinds with precise recovery.
